            ("p", "`class_name` renders as the HTML `class` attribute (avoiding the `class` keyword clash in Python); `style` takes a dict of CSS properties and renders as an inline `style` attribute. Built-in utility classes ship by default: `.nav`, `.card`, `.muted`, `.page`, `.hidden`."),
            ("code", "Text(\"Careful now\", class_name=\"muted\")\nContainer(..., style={\"background\": \"#f5f5ff\", \"padding\": \"1rem\"})"),
